{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Reuben, you are my firstborn.</b> He was worthy to receive three prerogatives: the birthright, the priesthood, and the kingship, and through his sin they were lost from him: the birthright was given to Joseph, the priesthood to Levi, and the kingship to Judah. And this is what he said, ״פחז כמים״ — and it is from the language of the Rabbis, blessed be their memory: ״עמא פחיזא״, ״אכתי בפחזותיכו קיימיתו״. Its meaning is that he was hasty in the way of impetuosity and light-mindedness, like waters that rush and flow. ״אל תותר״ — you shall not have that superiority which you were worthy of. And it is the birthright: ״בכורי אתה״. And the priesthood: ״יתר שאת״, from the language of the lifting of the hands, as it is written (Leviticus 10:17), ״ואותה נותן לכם לשאת את עון העדה״. And the kingship, this is what he said: ״יתר עז״ — the superiority of kingship, in the language of (I Samuel 2:10), ״ויתן עז למלכו״. And it is written (Psalms 99:4), ״ועז מלך משפט אהב״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The abbreviation רז\"ל has been expanded as 'the Rabbis, blessed be their memory' in the standard manner; the two Aramaic phrases are rendered as quotations without translation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:19.321084499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}